\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Leader of faithful souls, and Guide
\par Of all that travel to the sky,
\par Come and with us, even us, abide,
\par Who would on Thee alone rely,
\par On Thee alone our spirits stay,
\par While held in life's uneven way.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Strangers and pilgrims here below,
\par This earth, we know is not our place;
\par But hasten through the veil of woe,
\par And restless to behold Thy face,
\par Swift to our heavenly country move,
\par Our everlasting home above.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We have no abiding city here,
\par But seek a city out of sight;
\par Thither our study course as we steer,
\par Aspiring to the plains of light,
\par Jerusalem, the saints' abode,
\par Whose founder is the living God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Patient the appointed race to run,
\par This weary world we cast behind;
\par From strength to strength we travel on
\par The new Jerusalem to find;
\par Our labour this, our only aim,
\par To find the new Jerusalem.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Through Thee, who all our sins hast borne,
\par Freely and graciously forgiven,
\par With songs to Zion we return,
\par Contending for our native heaven;
\par That palace of our glorious King,
\par We find, it nearer while we sing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Raised by the breath of love divine,
\par We urge our way with strength renewed;
\par The church of the first-born to join,
\par We travel to the mount of God,
\par With joy upon our heads arise,
\par And meet our Captains in the skies.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

